From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 19:39:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(world): initialize and preserve Bedrock clock time

StartGame carries the day-cycle stop time, which is -1 while the cycle runs.
Using it as the initial clock position shows the wrong time until Bedrock sends
SetTime. Fall back to the level time for that initial packet and use the stop
time only when present.

Keep the full SetTime tick count in the Java world clock instead of reducing it
to one day, preserving day count and moon phase across sleep and time commands.

Track Bedrock clock initialization and state updates by ID and advance the Java clock from player tick age so later updates do not reset the client timeline.
